    "body": "Without an interface, every top-level binding in a module is exported, so the\ncompiler can never tell you one is unused. Adding a `.rei` turns warning 32 back\non \u2014 and it is a hard error under `--profile release`, which\n`deploy_branches.yml:69` gates on. So for these 12 modules, unused code now fails\nCI instead of accumulating.\n\nEach interface declares only the module's real external surface, so anything used\nsolely inside its own file becomes private. `JsUtil` alone hides 12 helpers\n(`date_now`, `find_scroll_container`, `QueryParams.get_arguments`, \u2026).\n\n264 lines of interface, 23 of them restated types.\n\n## Which 12\n\nPicked by how many lines of type declaration you would have to maintain in two\nplaces \u2014 not by file size:\n\n`ListUtil` 64 \u00b7 `JsUtil` 60 \u00b7 `StringUtil` 27 \u00b7 `Unicode` 25 \u00b7 `Tree` 23 \u00b7\n`OptUtil` 19 \u00b7 `Aba` 18 \u00b7 `VarMap` 9 \u00b7 `StructureShareSexp` 8 \u00b7 `Direction` 5 \u00b7\n`Either` 4 \u00b7 `FloatingElement` 2\n\n## What's excluded\n\n- **`Menu` (70 restated type lines) and `OpenRouter` (101).** Inline\n  `module M: { \u2026 } = { \u2026 }` sealing gets the same coverage with the signature\n  written once. `Id.re:142` already does it that way.\n- **`include <third-party>` modules** \u2014 `BigInt`, `Sets`, `Maps`, `MapUtil`,\n  `IntMap`, `Result`. `BigInt` is 14 source lines and extracts to 184; `refmt`\n  cannot parse it. Such an interface is a hand-copy of someone else's API that\n  breaks on their next release.\n- **`Util.re`**, which dune treats as the library interface module.\n\n## It found two dead functions immediately\n\n`Tree.equal_struct`, and then `Tree.equal` once that went. **The index-based\ndetector could not see either** \u2014 both match its `^equal` ppx-name suppression,\nwhich exists because ppx-generated call sites do not appear in the index at all.\nWorth knowing that the two tools miss different things.\n\n## Tooling\n\n`scripts/gen_rei.sh` / `make rei FILE=...` generates a starter interface:\n`ocamlc -i` over the ppx-expanded source dune already built, piped through\n`refmt`. Output is refmt-clean so `@src/fmt` accepts it. It strips the library's\nown alias prefix, since `-short-paths` renders siblings as `Util.Either.t`, which\nis a dependency cycle inside `src/util`.\n\nOne gotcha if you write one by hand: **a `.rei` can declare fewer derivers than\nthe `.re` and still compile**, because the ppx wraps generated values in\n`[@@@ocaml.warning \"-32\"]`. That drift only surfaces as `Unbound value` at a\nconsumer. Structural drift is caught immediately.\n\n## Verification\n\n`make test-quick`: 3,225 passing. dev, test and release builds clean \u2014 release is\nthe one that matters, since dev will not fail on the unused values a new interface\nexposes.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
